<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Korana</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as !Ora</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Korana are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khoekhoe">Khoikhoi</a> people of the interior of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, who moved north from the Cape into the Orange and Vaal river valleys in the 18th century. Living by herding, hunting and raiding on horseback, their groups fought Tswana, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/griqua">Griqua</a> and settler neighbours. In the 1880s the Korana chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Massouw rewarded white <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> with farms, which became the Republic of Stellaland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/korana.jpg" alt="Korana" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Neoneo13 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Korana_canyon_at_Slunj,_Croatia.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
